oox: let a text shape obey TextWordWrap when it is exported to DOCX (pdf-docx module only).

DrawingML::WriteText lets only a custom shape obey TextWordWrap; normal text always wraps (wrap="square"). The PDF import turns
word wrap off, on purpose, for a text box that holds a single line (pdfimport-singleline-nowrap-pdf-docx.patch), so in this
module a text shape obeys the property too and the box is written with wrap="none". Word then grows such a box sideways.
The DOCX branch that forces wrap="square" for a com.sun.star.drawing.TextShape (the PDF import's text boxes are TextShapes) skips a
shape whose TextWordWrap property itself is off, otherwise it would overwrite the "none". It reads the property, not the merged flag:
the tdf#134401 rule after it also turns wrapping off for any text shape with both auto-grow flags, which would make a box that the
importer left wrapping (more than one line) one long line too.
Routed to pdf-docx only; every other module keeps the rule. Not observed in Word.

diff --git a/oox/source/export/drawingml.cxx b/oox/source/export/drawingml.cxx
index 6deb9c3..ba75141 100644
--- a/oox/source/export/drawingml.cxx
+++ b/oox/source/export/drawingml.cxx
@@ -4189,10 +4189,17 @@ void DrawingML::WriteText(const Reference<XInterface>& rXIface, bool bBodyPr, bo
     bool bHasWrap = false;
     bool bWrap = false;
     // Only custom shapes obey the TextWordWrap option, normal text always wraps.
-    if (dynamic_cast<SvxCustomShape*>(rXIface.get()) && GetProperty(rXPropSet, u"TextWordWrap"_ustr))
+    // BUG-43 (pdf-docx module only, see the patch header): the PDF import turns word wrap off, on purpose, for a text box
+    // that holds a single line, so here a text shape obeys it too (wrap="none": Word grows the box sideways).
+    const bool bTextShapeWrap = xShape.is() && SdrObject::getSdrObjectFromXShape(xShape) != nullptr;
+    bool bTextShapeNoWrap = false;
+    if ((dynamic_cast<SvxCustomShape*>(rXIface.get()) || bTextShapeWrap) && GetProperty(rXPropSet, u"TextWordWrap"_ustr))
     {
         mAny >>= bWrap;
         bHasWrap = true;
+        // Only the property itself counts below: the tdf#134401 rule that follows also turns wrapping off for a text shape that
+        // merely has both auto-grow flags, and that would make every box (multi-line ones too) one long line.
+        bTextShapeNoWrap = bTextShapeWrap && !bWrap;
     }
 
     // tdf#134401: If AUTOGROWWIDTH and AUTOGROWHEIGHT are set, then export it as TextWordWrap
@@ -4220,8 +4227,10 @@ void DrawingML::WriteText(const Reference<XInterface>& rXIface, bool bBodyPr, bo
             // TextShape's automatic word wrapping, then we need to set
             // wrapping to square.
             uno::Reference<lang::XServiceInfo> xServiceInfo(rXIface, uno::UNO_QUERY);
-            if ((xServiceInfo.is() && xServiceInfo->supportsService(u"com.sun.star.drawing.TextShape"_ustr))
-                || bIsFontworkShape)
+            // BUG-43 (pdf-docx module only): a text shape whose word wrap the PDF import turned off keeps wrap="none".
+            if (!(bTextShapeNoWrap && !bIsFontworkShape)
+                && ((xServiceInfo.is() && xServiceInfo->supportsService(u"com.sun.star.drawing.TextShape"_ustr))
+                    || bIsFontworkShape))
                 pWrap = "square";
         }
 
